attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `folK`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 99.6% of them, at 0.20 bits {S1}.

@variable **The first fork is at `yadN`**, column 1, carried by 58% {S2.c1}. Columns 1 to 7, `yadN` to `yadC`, are [[fimbrial proteins and chaperones]], carried by 27 to 58%, the most plastic stretch of the window {S2, P, Q}. A branch of 3 persistent families runs through columns 76 to 78, [[arabinose and DNA metabolism]], carried by 10 to 16% {S8.b76}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 95 against 74%, and hesitates less there, 0.15 against 0.43 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 3, `htrE`, a fork column, 1.27 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Columns 75 to 79, `thiB` to `araC`, are carried by 71 to 89%, all persistent {S8}. The last column is `araC`, in 71% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 91% of genes**, 0.20 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.89 against 0.14 bits, and names fewer genes, 43% against 96% {C}.

